# Allow-list: send the Docker daemon only what the Dockerfile COPYs. Everything else (.git, .env,
# caches, tests, docs, CI config, local tooling) stays out of the build context, so builds are
# faster, the layer cache is not busted by unrelated edits, and secrets can never leak into an image.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!manage.py
!config
!common
!apps
!scripts/entrypoint.sh

# Test code, test settings and bytecode inside the allowed directories must not ship either.
**/tests
config/settings/test.py
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
